+++ b/docs/inventory-screen.md
@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Block inventory screen
+
+The screen where players see every block type, how many they have, which are locked and at what
+level they unlock, and pick the block to build with. Code: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/`,
+started by `InventoryScreen:Start()` in `Main.client.luau`. Stories: `ServerScriptService.Stories.Inventory`.
+
+## Player and moment
+
+- **Who:** mostly kids (assume ages 6 to 12) on a landscape phone; also PC and Xbox.
+- **When:** in the middle of building, to switch blocks or check what they have. The screen opens
+  only on request. Play is never blocked by it on join.
+- **Design-first device:** a 667 by 375 landscape phone.
+
+## Elements
+
+| Element | Job | How often it's needed |
+|---|---|---|
+| Inventory button (HUD) | Opens the panel; shows the block being built with | Always on screen |
+| Backdrop | Dims the world; tap or click it to close | While open |
+| Title "Blocks" | Says what the screen is | While open |
+| Close button (×) | Closes the panel, for touch, mouse, and gamepad focus | While open |
+| 10 block tiles | Color, name, count or lock + level; pick one | While open |
+| Details line | One sentence about the block under the pointer or focus, or the last refused tap | While open |
+| Gamepad hints (A Pick, B Close) | Shows the controller mapping | While open, gamepad only |
+
+## Where it sits
+
+| Element | Phone (touch) | Tablet (touch) | PC | Console / TV |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Inventory button | Top right, below the top bar, 80 × 80 | Same | Bottom center chip, 240 × 64, with **B** key cap | Bottom center chip with the **Y** glyph |
+| Panel | Centered, compact layout (96 tiles, details in the header) | Centered, regular layout | Centered, regular layout (120 tiles, details in a footer) | Same, scaled 1.25× on a 1080p TV |
+
+- The top right on touch stays clear of the thumbstick (left 40%, lower two thirds) and the jump
+  button (bottom right). On PC the top right belongs to the player list, so the button moves to the
+  bottom center there.
+- The ScreenGui uses `CoreUISafeInsets`. The whole UI grows with one `UIScale` on screens taller
+  than 1080. The panel shrinks to fit (never below 0.5), and phones get the compact layout (short
+  side under 600 UI units) instead of a shrunken one.
+- While the panel is open, Roblox's touch controls are hidden (`GuiService.TouchControlsEnabled`)
+  so the jump button doesn't sit on top of tiles, and `BlockPlacer` is disabled so a stray tap
+  can't place a block.
+
+## Opening and closing
+
+| | Open | Close |
+|---|---|---|
+| Touch | Tap the inventory button | Tap ×, tap the dimmed backdrop, tap the inventory button again, or pick a block |
+| Mouse and keyboard | Click the inventory button, or press **B** | Press **B**, click ×, click the backdrop, or pick a block |
+| Controller | Press **Y** | Press **B**, press **Y**, or pick a block |
+
+- Picking a block closes the panel right away, because switching blocks is the usual reason to
+  open it. The HUD button then shows the new block.
+- On a controller, focus starts on the tile of the block being built with. A `SelectionGroup` set
+  to `Stop` keeps focus inside the panel. B is bound at high priority through
+  `ContextActionService`. As a backup, the panel also closes if Roblox's own B handling clears
+  gamepad focus first.
+
+## Actions
+
+| Action | Touch | Mouse and keyboard | Controller |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| See counts and locks | Shown on every tile: the count, or 🔒 and "Level N" | Same | Same |
+| Read details | Tap a locked or empty tile; the details line explains it | Hover a tile | Move focus with the D-pad or stick |
+| Pick a block | Tap an available tile | Click it, or press its number key (1 to 9, 0); each tile shows its key | Press **A** on the focused tile |
+| Refused pick (locked or none left) | Tile shakes; details line says why ("Reach level 4 to unlock Ice. You're level 3.") | Same | Same |
+| Close | See above | See above | See above |
+
+No information needs hover: every hover detail also shows on focus and on tap.
+
+## Tile states
+
+| State | How it looks (never color alone) |
+|---|---|
+| Available | Block color swatch, name, count in white |
+| Hover / focus | Lighter tile; a white focus ring on controller |
+| Pressed | Darker tile, contents sink 2 px |
+| Selected (building with it) | Yellow inner outline **and** a check-mark badge |
+| Empty (0 held) | Faded swatch, gray text, count "0"; a tap explains how to get some |
+| Locked | Grayed swatch with 🔒, gray text, "Level N" in place of the count |
+| Large counts | 10,000 and up show as "12K" |
+
+## Motion
+
+| Animation | Timing | Reduced motion (`ReducedMotionEnabled`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Panel opens | Backdrop fades in, panel slides up 24 px; critically damped spring, about 0.25 s | Fade only, no slide |
+| Panel closes | Reverse, removed after 0.2 s | Fade only |
+| Press | Color change and 2 px sink, immediate | Same (no movement beyond 2 px) |
+| Refused pick | Short horizontal shake | No shake; the details line still explains |
+
+Backgrounds follow the player's Background Transparency setting (`PreferredTransparency`).
+
+## Accessibility notes and exceptions
+
+- Text is 16 to 32 px at 1080p on light-on-dark surfaces; body text clears 4.5:1 contrast.
+- Touch targets are at least 80 (HUD), 96 (tiles), and 48 (close) UI units.
+- **Exception:** tile labels have fixed heights. At the Largest text size, a long name may be cut
+  off with "…". The details line shows the full name. Check this in the emulator.
+- **Exception:** on the compact (phone) layout, the gamepad A/B hints are left out to save room.
+
+## Open questions (playtest or funnel tasks)
+
+1. Should picking close the panel, or keep it open? Watch five new players switch blocks twice.
+2. Do kids find the top-right button on phones? Log `inventory_opened` with the input type, and
+   the time from first join to first open.
+3. Do players understand locked tiles? Log `inventory_pick_refused` with the reason. Many repeated
+   taps on the same locked tile would mean the message isn't landing.
+4. Is **B** a good PC key, or do players look for **E** or **Tab**?
+
+## Known gaps outside this screen
+
+- Number keys in `BlockPlacer` can still select locked or empty blocks. The panel refuses them,
+  but the hotkeys don't. The server doesn't check level or count either.
+- `BlockPlacer` places blocks only with mouse clicks and screen taps, so controller players can
+  pick a block here but have no way to place it yet.
